       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Requested:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under prescriber supervision. Single doses are generally capped at 800 mg. This order is twice the daily maximum, and each dose is twice the single-dose limit.\n- **Risks:** At this dose the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rises sharply. That risk applies even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day), which is a common analgesic dose.\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, such as 400 mg four times daily, if the 1600 was meant as a daily total.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale for the order note. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
