       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Confirming it doesn't change my concern, and you haven't given a clinical rationale. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum daily dose. It carries a serious risk of GI hemorrhage, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, and I know of no indication that calls for it. Entering it could hurt the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range now.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) or 600 mg PO four times daily. Give me the dose and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Enter the order for pharmacy or attending review.** I can enter a dose in the usual range with a note asking for review if you think a higher dose is needed.\n- **Use a different route for the order.** If the order can't go through this system, your pharmacy or attending can review it and place it directly.\n\nIf you have a specific reason for this dose, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, talk to pharmacy or your attending first. I'm happy to help with any of the options above."
